{{ =================================================================================================

   File....... SD_soft_la_test.spin2
   Purpose.... P2-internal "software logic analyzer" for the SD bus. A spare
               cog's streamer captures one SD signal at a time while the
               driver performs a sector read, so we can see -- in software,
               no external instrument -- what is actually on the wire during
               the failing streamer-DMA read.
   Author..... Stephen M Moraco
               -- see below for terms of use
   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
   Started.... 18 MAY 2026

   =================================================================================================
   THEORY OF OPERATION
   =================================================================================================

   WHY THIS EXISTS

     The Cloudisk 2GB SDSC card reads correctly via the driver's slow,
     byte-by-byte path but returns NOTHING via the streamer-DMA path
     (the streamer leaves the destination buffer untouched). Phase and SPI
     clock rate were ruled out by earlier diagnostics. The one remaining
     question can only be answered by observing the bus during a streamer
     read:
       1. Does SCK actually toggle during the streamer burst?
       2. Does the card drive MISO with the sector data in response?

   WHY ONE SIGNAL AT A TIME (SEQUENTIAL, NOT SIMULTANEOUS)

     A simultaneous four-signal capture would need the streamer's 16-pin
     capture mode, whose only block-aligned window containing both MISO
     (P58) and SCK (P61) is P48..P63 -- which also contains P62/P63, the
     P2's debug-serial pins. A capture spanning those pins corrupts the
     very channel this tool reports through.

     The fix is to NOT capture them together. Each question above is a
     self-contained yes/no:
       - "Does SCK toggle?" -> capture SCK alone, count transitions.
       - "Does the card drive MISO?" -> capture MISO alone; a real 512-byte
         read shows ~164 us of dense toggling, unmistakable on its own with
         no clock correlation required.
     So this tool captures ONE pin per SD read, sequentially. Each capture
     uses the streamer's 1-pin mode (X_1P_1DAC1_WFBYTE) -- the exact mode
     the driver itself uses for sector reads, proven not to disturb other
     pins. P58 and P61 are nowhere near the P62/P63 debug pins.

   NO DEBUG DURING A CAPTURE

     `debug()` transmits on P62. To guarantee the debug channel and a
     running capture never interact, this tool emits NO debug output
     between launching a capture cog and that capture completing. All
     results for a capture are printed only after the capture cog has
     finished and stopped.

   MECHANISM

     A spare cog (cogspin of a Spin2 method, so DAT vars resolve; the
     streamer work is inline PASM) captures the selected pin with two
     back-to-back XINITs against one continuous WRFAST. 1-pin capture packs
     8 samples per byte, so the hub write rate is ~22 MB/s.

   HARDWARE-EDGE TRIGGER (CS)

     A software-timed capture window can miss the read: readSectorRaw goes
     through the worker-cog mailbox, so the bus activity starts an
     indeterminate handoff later. Instead, the capture cog sets the
     streamer up, then spins on CS (P60) and issues XINIT only when CS
     FALLS -- the real start of the SD transaction. The capture is thus
     synced to the bus event itself, not to the software call. (An earlier
     waitus()-windowed version missed the read; the symptom was a capture
     showing ~50 SCK transitions, far too few for any real transaction.)

   SAMPLE RATE AND NYQUIST

     Sample clock = sysclk/2 (streamer NCO xfrq = $8000_0000). At
     _CLKFREQ = 350 MHz that is 175 MS/s -- 7 samples per 25 MHz SCK
     period, 3.5x the Nyquist rate. Window = 128000 samples = ~731 us,
     which contains a full 25 MHz single-sector read.

   READING THE RESULT

     - SCK shows thousands of transitions  -> SCK is clocking.
       SCK essentially static               -> driver clock-gen (WYPIN) dead.
     - MISO shows a long dense burst of transitions -> the card IS driving
       the sector data; with the driver's streamer buffer coming back
       empty, the bug is in the driver's streamer-RX capture path.
       MISO flat -> the card does not drive MISO under streamer clocking
       (a card limitation).

   LIMITATION

     This records the digital logic level the P2 input registers latch.
     It does not reveal analog signal quality (slow slew, marginal levels).
     If the streamer fails because MISO slews too slowly to latch cleanly,
     a scope is still required for that residual question.

================================================================================================= }}

CON

    _CLKFREQ        = 350_000_000

    DEBUG_BAUD      = 2_000_000

    ' P2 Edge module SD slot pins
    SD_CS   = 60
    SD_MOSI = 59
    SD_MISO = 58
    SD_SCK  = 61

    ' Streamer 1-pin capture: X_1P_1DAC1_WFBYTE (mode %1100) + write-enable
    ' (D[23]). The captured pin number is OR'd in as (pin << 17); the low
    ' 16 bits carry the sample count. 8 samples pack into each hub byte.
    CAP_1P_BASE       = $C000_0000 | $0080_0000                                 ' = $C080_0000
    ' Streamer NCO (P2KB p2kbPasm2Setxfrq): D = target_freq * 2^32 / clkfreq.
    ' sysclk/2 sample rate -> D = 2^32 / 2 = $8000_0000.
    CAP_XFRQ          = $8000_0000                                              ' sysclk/2 = 175 MS/s at 350 MHz

    SAMPLES_PER_XINIT = 64000                                                   ' multiple of 8; < 16-bit count max
    NUM_XINIT         = 2
    TOTAL_SAMPLES     = SAMPLES_PER_XINIT * NUM_XINIT                           ' 128000
    CAP_BUF_BYTES     = TOTAL_SAMPLES / 8                                       ' 16000

    WAVE_SNIPPET      = 96                                                      ' samples shown in ASCII waveform

#ifdef __SPINTOOLS__
#define SD_INCLUDE_ALL
#elseifdef __FLEXSPIN__
#define SD_INCLUDE_ALL
#pragma exportdef SD_INCLUDE_ALL
#else
#pragma exportdef SD_INCLUDE_ALL
#endif

OBJ
    sd : "micro_sd_fat32_fs"

DAT
    capBuf      BYTE    0[CAP_BUF_BYTES]                                        ' bit-packed capture buffer
    scratchBuf  BYTE    0[512]                                                  ' SD read destination
    rowBuf      BYTE    0[WAVE_SNIPPET + 1]                                     ' one waveform row, assembled then printed
    capStack    LONG    0[64]                                                   ' capture cog stack
    capModeWord LONG    0                                                       ' main -> capture cog: streamer mode | pin | count
    capStarted  LONG    0                                                       ' capture cog -> main: streamer running
    capDone     LONG    0                                                       ' capture cog -> main: capture complete

    sckTrans    LONG    0                                                       ' kept for the cross-capture verdict
    misoTrans   LONG    0

PUB go() | status

    debug(" ")
    debug("=== SD SOFT LOGIC ANALYZER (sequential 1-pin captures) ===")
    debug("  Sample rate sysclk/2 = ", udec_(clkfreq / 2_000_000), " MS/s   window ", udec_((TOTAL_SAMPLES * 2) / (clkfreq / 1_000_000)), " us")
    debug("  No debug is emitted while a capture is running.")
    debug(" ")

    status := sd.initCardOnly(SD_CS, SD_MOSI, SD_MISO, SD_SCK)
    if status < 0
        debug("FATAL: initCardOnly failed (", sdec_(status), ") - power-cycle the card and retry.")
        debug("END_SESSION")
        return
    debug("  initCardOnly OK (cls=", udec_((sd.getOCR() >> 30) & 1), " 0=SDSC,1=SDHC)")
    debug(" ")

    ' --- Capture 1: SCK during a streamer read ---
    debug("------------------------------------------------------------")
    debug("CAPTURE 1: SCK (P61) during a streamer-DMA read of sector 0")
    debug("------------------------------------------------------------")
    capture1pin(@"SCK", SD_SCK, true)

    ' --- Capture 2: MISO during a streamer read ---
    debug(" ")
    debug("------------------------------------------------------------")
    debug("CAPTURE 2: MISO (P58) during a streamer-DMA read of sector 0")
    debug("------------------------------------------------------------")
    capture1pin(@"MISO", SD_MISO, false)

    ' --- Cross-capture verdict ---
    debug(" ")
    debug("============================================================")
    debug("  VERDICT")
    debug("============================================================")
    if sckTrans < 1000
        debug("  SCK did NOT clock during the read (", udec_(sckTrans), " transitions).")
        debug("  -> The driver's streamer clock generation (WYPIN) is not running.")
    elseif misoTrans < 50
        debug("  SCK clocked (", udec_(sckTrans), " transitions) but MISO stayed flat")
        debug("  (", udec_(misoTrans), " transitions).")
        debug("  -> The card does not drive MISO under continuous streamer")
        debug("     clocking. This is a card limitation, not a driver bug.")
    else
        debug("  SCK clocked (", udec_(sckTrans), " transitions) AND MISO carried")
        debug("  data (", udec_(misoTrans), " transitions) during the read, yet the")
        debug("  driver's streamer buffer came back empty.")
        debug("  -> The card and the wire are fine. The bug is in the driver's")
        debug("     streamer-RX capture path itself.")
    debug(" ")
    debug("END_SESSION")


PRI capture1pin(p_label, pin, isSck) | status, cogN, t0
' Capture one pin for the duration of one streamer-DMA sector read.
' CRITICAL: between launching the capture cog and the capture completing,
' this routine emits NO debug() output (debug transmits on P62).

    capStarted := 0
    capDone := 0
    bytefill(@capBuf, 0, CAP_BUF_BYTES)
    bytefill(@scratchBuf, $EE, 512)
    capModeWord := CAP_1P_BASE | (pin << 17) | SAMPLES_PER_XINIT

    cogN := cogspin(NEWCOG, captureCog(), @capStack)
    if cogN < 0 or cogN > 7
        debug("  ERROR: could not launch capture cog (", sdec_(cogN), ")")
        return

    ' ---- quiet zone: no debug() from here until the capture has finished ----
    t0 := getms()
    repeat until capStarted
        if getms() - t0 > 200
            debug("  ERROR: capture cog never signaled start")
            return

    waitus(5)                                                                   ' ensure the capture cog reached its CS-poll loop

    status := sd.readSectorRaw(0, @scratchBuf)                                  ' the SD read; its CS edge triggers the capture

    t0 := getms()
    repeat until capDone
        if getms() - t0 > 500
            debug("  ERROR: capture did not complete within 500ms")
            return
    ' ---- end quiet zone: capture cog has finished and stopped ----

    debug("  capture cog ran on cog ", udec_(cogN))
    debug("  driver streamer read status=", sdec_(status), "  buf[0..3]=$", uhex_byte_(scratchBuf[0]), " $", uhex_byte_(scratchBuf[1]), " $", uhex_byte_(scratchBuf[2]), " $", uhex_byte_(scratchBuf[3]))
    analyze1pin(p_label, isSck)


PRI analyze1pin(p_label, isSck) | idx, level, prev, trans, firstTrans, lastTrans, highs

' Unpack the bit-packed capture, count transitions and high/low balance,
' locate the active region, print a summary and an ASCII waveform snippet.

    trans      := 0
    firstTrans := -1
    lastTrans  := -1
    highs      := 0
    prev       := (capBuf[0] >> 0) & 1

    repeat idx from 1 to TOTAL_SAMPLES - 1
        level := (capBuf[idx >> 3] >> (idx & 7)) & 1
        if level
            highs++
        if level <> prev
            trans++
            if firstTrans < 0
                firstTrans := idx
            lastTrans := idx
        prev := level

    debug(" ")
    debug("  ANALYSIS: ", zstr_(p_label))
    debug("    samples: ", udec_(TOTAL_SAMPLES), "   transitions: ", udec_(trans))
    debug("    high samples: ", udec_(highs), " / ", udec_(TOTAL_SAMPLES))
    if firstTrans < 0
        debug("    signal is STATIC for the entire capture (no transitions).")
    else
        debug("    active region: sample ", udec_(firstTrans), "..", udec_(lastTrans), "  (", udec_(((lastTrans - firstTrans) * 2) / (clkfreq / 1_000_000)), " us span)")

    if isSck
        sckTrans := trans
        if trans < 1000
            debug("    -> SCK is STATIC / barely clocking.")
        else
            debug("    -> SCK is CLOCKING.")
    else
        misoTrans := trans
        if trans < 50
            debug("    -> MISO is essentially flat - the card is not driving data.")
        else
            debug("    -> MISO is CARRYING DATA (sustained transitions).")

    if firstTrans >= 0
        printWaveform(firstTrans)


PRI printWaveform(startIdx) | lineEnd
' Print a WAVE_SNIPPET-sample ASCII view of the captured signal.

    lineEnd := startIdx + WAVE_SNIPPET - 1
    if lineEnd > TOTAL_SAMPLES - 1
        lineEnd := TOTAL_SAMPLES - 1
    debug("    waveform from sample ", udec_(startIdx), " (1 char = 1 sample = ", udec_((2 * 1_000) / (clkfreq / 1_000_000)), " ns):")
    debug_char_row(@"    sig : ", startIdx, lineEnd)


PRI debug_char_row(p_prefix, startIdx, lineEnd) | idx, p_dst
' Assemble the captured signal as a row of 0/1 characters, print on one line.

    p_dst := @rowBuf
    repeat idx from startIdx to lineEnd
        BYTE[p_dst++] := ((capBuf[idx >> 3] >> (idx & 7)) & 1) ? "1" : "0"
    BYTE[p_dst] := 0
    debug(zstr_(p_prefix), zstr_(@rowBuf))


PRI captureCog() | mode1, bufAddr, xf
' Runs on its own cog (a Spin2 method, so DAT vars resolve correctly; the
' streamer work is inline PASM, the same pattern the driver uses). Reads
' capModeWord, captures the selected pin with two back-to-back XINITs
' against one continuous WRFAST, then signals completion.

    mode1   := capModeWord
    bufAddr := @capBuf
    xf      := CAP_XFRQ
    capStarted := 1                                                             ' signal main cog: armed, watching CS

    ' Hardware-edge trigger: set the streamer up, then wait for CS (P60) to
    ' fall -- the real start of the SD transaction -- before XINIT. This
    ' syncs the capture to the bus event itself, not to the software call.
    org
                setxfrq xf                                                      ' sample clock = sysclk/2
                wrfast  #0, bufAddr                                             ' FIFO -> capBuf, continuous
waitCsLow       testp   #SD_CS  wc                                              ' C = CS pin level (1=idle high)
        if_c    jmp     #waitCsLow                                              ' spin while CS is high
                xinit   mode1, #0                                               ' CS just fell -> capture first batch
                waitxfi
                xinit   mode1, #0                                               ' capture next batch (FIFO continues)
                waitxfi
    end

    capDone := 1                                                                ' signal main cog: capture complete


con { license }

